# SOLID Principles for gRPC Server

## Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)
- Each service should handle only one business domain (e.g., UserService, OrderService)
- Separate concerns: [cmd/main.go](mdc:cmd/main.go) handles CLI, [cmd/commands/start.go](mdc:cmd/commands/start.go) handles server startup
- Create dedicated files for each responsibility:
  - `internal/service/` - Business logic implementation
  - `internal/repository/` - Data access layer
  - `internal/handler/` - gRPC handlers
  - `internal/config/` - Configuration management

## Open/Closed Principle (OCP)
- Use interfaces for service contracts
- Implement plugin architecture for extending functionality
- Example: Create `UserServiceInterface` that can be extended without modifying existing code

## Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP)
- All implementations of an interface should be interchangeable
- Mock implementations should behave consistently with real implementations
- Database and in-memory repositories should implement the same interface

## Interface Segregation Principle (ISP)
- Create small, focused interfaces rather than large monolithic ones
- Separate read and write operations: `UserReader`, `UserWriter`
- Avoid forcing clients to depend on methods they don't use

## Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP)
- Depend on abstractions, not concretions
- Inject dependencies through constructors
- Use dependency injection container for complex applications
- High-level modules should not depend on low-level modules

## Implementation Guidelines

### Service Layer Structure
```go
// Good: Interface-based design
type UserService interface {
    GetUser(ctx context.Context, id string) (*User, error)
    CreateUser(ctx context.Context, user *User) error
}

type userService struct {
    repo UserRepository
    validator UserValidator
    logger Logger
}
```

### Repository Pattern
```go
type UserRepository interface {
    FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*User, error)
    Save(ctx context.Context, user *User) error
}
```

### Handler Layer
```go
type UserHandler struct {
    service UserService
}

func (h *UserHandler) GetUser(ctx context.Context, req *pb.GetUserRequest) (*pb.GetUserResponse, error) {
    // Delegate to service layer
}
```
